{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Take for yourself a calf.</b> In Yoma 3a they raised a fine point: after it says ״ואל בני ישראל״ etc., why do I need ״קח לך״? It is self-understood that the calf is his. And they interpreted that it comes to say that he should take from his own and not from the public's." "Further, it appears possible to say that the saying of ״לך״ is because this will be for him an everlasting sign that he did not make the calf with intention, heaven forbid, and did not stray after it; rather, it came about through him unintentionally and without evil thought. From this perspective the calf can effect atonement for him, which is not the case for Israel, since their act with the calf has the aspect of intentional sin, and the calf will not come as a sin-offering for them — on the contrary, it is a prosecutor (katigor). And you will find (Leviticus Rabbah 21:10) that HaShem insisted that Aharon not enter the innermost Sanctuary of the House of HaShem on Yom HaKippurim in golden garments, because he made the gold of the calf." "And one must raise a difficulty here: why did HaShem command that he bring a calf of cattle for a sin-offering, when a sin-offering comes for atonement and there is no defender (sanigor) in the world like it? And it appears that the Master, blessed be He, judged the matter with justice, because Aharon performed no act in the aspect of the making of the calf: he did not form it nor prepare it, and needless to say he did not believe in it and did not stray after it, heaven forbid, as he said to Mosheh (Exodus 32:24) ״ויצא העגל״ — meaning, it came out on its own through an act performed by two sorcerers of the mixed multitude, Yunos and Yombrus, as they of blessed memory said (Tanhuma, Ki Tisa 19). From this it follows that the act he performed was only in the aspect of the gold, of which he said to them (ibid.) ״למי זהב התפרקו״, and he took it from their hand and formed it with a graving tool — and this act he did with full knowledge. And although his motive was out of fear of Israel, lest they kill him as they killed Ḥur, and he was also wasting time for them until Mosheh would come, even so, he performed an improper act. Therefore HaShem said that he should bring the calf to atone for the matter that came about through him unintentionally. But the gold — with the act he performed in it, that was with deliberate intent — HaShem said it shall not be seen in the inner sanctum, so that a prosecutor (katigor) not become a defender (sanigor). Whereas Israel, who sinned with the calf, cannot bring a calf for atonement; therefore HaShem commanded that they bring a goat." "<b>Further,</b> it appears possible to raise the point: how do we say (Rosh HaShanah 26a) ״a prosecutor (katigor) does not become a defender (sanigor)״ regarding the matter of gold, when they said (Arakhin 16a) that the four golden garments of the Kohen Gadol atone for four types of transgressions etc. — if so, is the prosecutor becoming the defender? And necessarily one must resolve that the mode of atonement in the outer sanctuary differs from the atonement of the inner sanctum, for the atonement of the inner sanctum whitens sins like snow — and this is your sign: the tongue of crimson wool (Yoma 67a) — and this matter is wondrous and requires that no trace of the transgression be found in it at all. Therefore the garments, by being in the outer sanctuary, do effect atonement, despite being of the category of gold, which is not the case with the atonement of the inner sanctum. And also according to this distinction, Aharon's sin regarding the gold differs from Israel's sin regarding the calf: Aharon atones in the outer sanctuary with golden garments, while Israel are not atoned through the calf, because Aharon's sin regarding the gold was complete inadvertence in his taking of it and his placing it in the mold, which is not the case with Israel. Therefore they will not be atoned through the calf even in the outer sanctuary. Understand:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:54:39.301253578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}